IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-cgt`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- the indexed cost base from 1 July 2027, worked out element by
-- element: s 110-25 (the five elements), s 110-36(1A), Division 114 (ss 114-1(1), 114-10, 114-25, 114-30) and Subdivision
-- 960-M (ss 960-270, 960-275(1B), (1C), (4), (5), 960-280(1)), with the capital gain under s 104-10(4).
--
-- A module beside itaa-cgt.l4 (REQ-0057, 22 October 2026). itaa-cgt.l4 takes the indexation factor as a supplied number and
-- multiplies the whole cost base by it ("Simplified"); it stays as it is. This module works the factor out from the index
-- numbers and indexes each piece of expenditure by its own factor, leaving the third element out. It calls itaa-cgt.l4's
-- `Is my cost base indexed` (s 110-36(1A), s 114-10) rather than restating it.
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- an individual Australian resident who sells shares or another CGT asset on or after 1 July 2027
-- ("What is my indexed cost base, and so my capital gain?"). Daniel d071 and Chloe c085 (both 30 June 2050).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00400, 12 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt. The s 960-275 formulas are images
-- the text deposit dropped; they are transcribed from Volume 10 of the Word rendering of the same compilation in
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.formulas.md (2026-10-22), and encoded from there.
--
-- INPUTS THAT ARE NOT LAW. s 960-280(1): the index number for a quarter is "the All Groups Consumer Price Index number (being
-- the weighted average of the 8 capital cities) first published by the Australian Statistician for the quarter". Those
-- numbers are published facts, and for the lives' quarters (2031 to 2050) future ones, so each is an input: the person states
-- the index number for the quarter of the CGT event and for the quarter in which each amount was incurred or paid.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Expenditure incurred before 1 July 2027 (s 960-275(1B)(b)) -- for an asset held on 30 June 2027 that needs
-- Subdivision 112-E's deemed sale and reacquisition, and otherwise it is not indexed under (1B): such an item answers
-- `not covered`; indexation under s 110-36(1) (assets acquired before 21 September 1999; s 960-275(2), (3)); the cost base
-- modifications and when expenditure is incurred for them (ss 114-15, 114-20, Division 112); a change of the CPI reference
-- period (s 960-280(3)) -- the index numbers given are taken to be in one reference period; capital losses and the reduced
-- cost base (indexation is not relevant to it, s 114-5 Note 2); trusts and beneficiaries (Subdiv 115-C). Dates are written
-- YYYYMMDD, as in itaa-cgt.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- the indexed cost base from 1 July 2027`

§§ `110-25 -- the five elements of the cost base`

-- s 110-25(1): "The cost base of a *CGT asset consists of 5 elements." (2) the first is the money paid and the market value of
-- property given "in respect of *acquiring it"; (3) the second is "the *incidental costs you incurred"; (4) the third is "the
-- costs of owning the *CGT asset you incurred" (interest, maintenance, repairs, insurance, rates, land tax); (5) the fourth is
-- capital expenditure "the purpose or the expected effect of which is to increase or preserve the asset's value" or "that relates
-- to installing or moving the asset"; (6) the fifth is "capital expenditure that you incurred to establish, preserve or defend
-- your title to the asset, or a right over the asset".
DECLARE `Cost base element` IS ONE OF
    `the first element: acquiring the asset`
    `the second element: incidental costs`
    `the third element: costs of owning the asset`
    `the fourth element: capital expenditure on the asset's value`
    `the fifth element: capital expenditure on title`

-- s 960-275 indexes expenditure from the quarter in which it was incurred ((1B)), except that an amount in the first element of a
-- share or unit "paid to the company or trust at a time: (a) after the asset was *acquired" is indexed from the quarter in which
-- it is paid ((1C)) -- a call on a partly-paid share, for example (the s 960-275 Example).
DECLARE `Kind of amount` IS ONE OF
    `expenditure incurred in the element`
    `an amount paid to the company or trust on a share or unit after acquiring it`

-- One amount in the cost base: its element, how much, when it was incurred (or, for the second kind, paid), and the index
-- number (s 960-280(1)) for the quarter in which that date falls (s 995-1: quarters end on 31 March, 30 June, 30 September and
-- 31 December).
DECLARE `Cost base amount` HAS
    `element` IS A `Cost base element`
    `kind` IS A `Kind of amount`
    `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `incurred or paid on` IS A NUMBER
    `index number for its quarter` IS A NUMBER

§§ `960-275(1B), (1C), (5) -- the indexation factor`

-- s 960-275(1B), from the authorised rendering (C2004A05138.formulas.md):
--     Index number for the quarter in which the *CGT event happens / Index number for the quarter in which the expenditure is incurred
-- s 960-275(1C): the same, with "the quarter in which the amount is paid" below the bar.
-- s 960-275(5): "You work out the *indexation factor to 3 decimal places (rounding up if the fourth decimal place is 5 or more)."
-- Example in (5): "If the factor is 1.102795, it would be rounded up to 1.103."
@export What is the indexation factor for an amount in my cost base (s 960-275(1B), (1C), (5))?
GIVEN `index number for the quarter of the CGT event` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number first published for the quarter in which you sold the asset (or the CGT event happened)
      `index number for the quarter of the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number first published for the quarter in which you incurred the expenditure (or paid the amount to the company)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the indexation factor` MEANS
    FLOOR ((`index number for the quarter of the CGT event` DIVIDED BY `index number for the quarter of the amount`) TIMES 1000 PLUS 0.5)
        DIVIDED BY 1000

§§ `960-270, 960-275(4), 114-1(1) -- indexing one amount`

-- The answer for one amount: indexed (with its factor), left as it is (with the reason), or outside this module.
DECLARE `Indexing an amount` IS ONE OF
    `indexed` HAS `factor` IS A NUMBER
                  `indexed amount` IS A NUMBER
    `not indexed: the third element (s 960-275(4))` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `not indexed: the factor is 1 or less (s 960-270(2))` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: incurred or paid before 1 July 2027 (Subdivision 112-E and s 960-275(2), (3) are not encoded)`
    `not covered: paid to the company before or when the asset was acquired, so not a (1C) amount`

-- s 114-1(1): "In working out the *cost base of a *CGT asset under subsection 110-36(1A), index expenditure incurred in each
-- element (except the third element)." s 960-275(4): "However, you cannot index expenditure in the third element of the *cost base
-- of a CGT asset (costs of ownership)." s 960-270(1): "You index an amount by multiplying it by its *indexation factor." (2): "You
-- do not index the amount if its *indexation factor is 1 or less." (1B)(b) and (1C)(b): incurred or paid "on or after 1 July
-- 2027"; (1C)(a) "after the asset was *acquired". (1C) applies only to "the first element of the *cost base of a *CGT asset that
-- is a *share in a company, or unit in a unit trust": an amount of that kind is taken to be one.
GIVEN `a` IS A `Cost base amount`
      `acquired on` IS A NUMBER
      `index number for the quarter of the CGT event` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Indexing an amount`
`indexing` MEANS
    IF `a`'s `element` EQUALS `the third element: costs of owning the asset`
    THEN `not indexed: the third element (s 960-275(4))` (`a`'s `amount`)
    ELSE IF `a`'s `incurred or paid on` LESS THAN 20270701
         THEN `not covered: incurred or paid before 1 July 2027 (Subdivision 112-E and s 960-275(2), (3) are not encoded)`
         ELSE IF     `a`'s `kind` EQUALS `an amount paid to the company or trust on a share or unit after acquiring it`
                 AND `a`'s `incurred or paid on` AT MOST `acquired on`
              THEN `not covered: paid to the company before or when the asset was acquired, so not a (1C) amount`
              ELSE IF `the factor` AT MOST 1
                   THEN `not indexed: the factor is 1 or less (s 960-270(2))` (`a`'s `amount`)
                   ELSE `indexed` `the factor` (`a`'s `amount` TIMES `the factor`)
    WHERE
        `the factor` MEANS `What is the indexation factor` `index number for the quarter of the CGT event` (`a`'s `index number for its quarter`)

§§ `110-36(1A) -- the cost base, indexed element by element`

-- The answer for the whole cost base or the gain: a dollar figure, or outside this module because one of its amounts is.
DECLARE `Indexed answer` IS ONE OF
    `dollars` HAS `value` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: an amount in the cost base was incurred or paid before 1 July 2027, or is not a (1C) amount`

GIVEN `i` IS AN `Indexing an amount`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount counted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `i`
    WHEN `indexed` `f` `x` THEN JUST `x`
    WHEN `not indexed: the third element (s 960-275(4))` `x` THEN JUST `x`
    WHEN `not indexed: the factor is 1 or less (s 960-270(2))` `x` THEN JUST `x`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `xs` IS A LIST OF MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the total of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `xs`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `x` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        CONSIDER `x`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `v` THEN
            CONSIDER `the total of` `rest`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST `t` THEN JUST (`v` PLUS `t`)

GIVEN `a` IS A `Cost base amount`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`its plain amount` MEANS `a`'s `amount`

-- s 110-36(1A): "The cost base of a *CGT asset also includes indexation of the elements of the cost base (except the third
-- element) for the purposes of working out the *capital gain of an individual or a trust from a *CGT event happening in relation
-- to the CGT asset if: (a) the CGT event happens on or after 1 July 2027; and (b) the requirements of Division 114 are met."
-- Division 114's requirements, for an individual: s 114-10(1) (acquired at least 12 months before the event) and s 114-25(2)
-- (neither a foreign resident nor a temporary resident at any time from the later of 1 July 2027 and acquisition to the event),
-- both through itaa-cgt.l4's `Is my cost base indexed`; and s 114-30(2), the asset is not one "for which either of the
-- following sections applies in relation to the *capital gain: (a) section 115-102 (about new residential dwellings); (b)
-- section 115-125 (about affordable housing)". Where indexation is not included, the cost base is the plain sum.
GIVEN `foreign or temporary resident in the testing period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 115-102 or 115-125 applies to the gain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acquired on` IS A NUMBER
      `event on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`indexation is included for an individual` MEANS
        `Is my cost base indexed` `an individual` `foreign or temporary resident in the testing period` `acquired on` `event on`
    AND (NOT `section 115-102 or 115-125 applies to the gain`)

@export What is my cost base, indexed element by element where s 110-36(1A) applies (ss 110-25, 110-36(1A), 114-1, 960-275)?
GIVEN `foreign or temporary resident in the testing period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at any time from 1 July 2027 (or from when you acquired the asset, if later) until the sale you were a foreign resident or a temporary resident
      `section 115-102 or 115-125 applies to the gain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the asset is a new residential dwelling or affordable housing whose gain keeps the discount under s 115-102 or s 115-125
      `acquired on` IS A NUMBER @desc When you acquired the asset (YYYYMMDD)
      `event on` IS A NUMBER @desc When you sold it, or the CGT event happened (YYYYMMDD)
      `index number for the quarter of the CGT event` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number first published for the quarter of the sale
      `amounts` IS A LIST OF `Cost base amount` @desc Each amount in your cost base: its element, whether it is a later payment to the company on a share, how much, when you incurred or paid it (YYYYMMDD), and the CPI number for that quarter
GIVETH AN `Indexed answer`
`What is my indexed cost base` MEANS
    IF `indexation is included for an individual` `foreign or temporary resident in the testing period` `section 115-102 or 115-125 applies to the gain` `acquired on` `event on`
    THEN CONSIDER `the total of` (map `counted` `amounts`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered: an amount in the cost base was incurred or paid before 1 July 2027, or is not a (1C) amount`
         WHEN JUST `t` THEN `dollars` `t`
    ELSE `dollars` (sum (map `its plain amount` `amounts`))
    WHERE
        `counted` `a` MEANS `the amount counted` (`indexing` `a` `acquired on` `index number for the quarter of the CGT event`)

§§ `104-10(4) -- the capital gain on the indexed cost base`

-- s 104-10(4) (CGT event A1): "You make a capital gain if the *capital proceeds from the disposal are more than the asset's *cost
-- base." The gain is the excess; otherwise nil here (a capital loss turns on the reduced cost base, not encoded). A gain worked
-- out with indexation is not a discount capital gain (s 115-20), and an individual's discount percentage for a CGT event on or
-- after 1 July 2027 is 0% (s 115-100(f)) -- see itaa-cgt.l4.
@export What is my capital gain on the cost base indexed element by element (ss 104-10(4), 110-36(1A), 960-275)?
GIVEN `foreign or temporary resident in the testing period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at any time from 1 July 2027 (or from when you acquired the asset, if later) until the sale you were a foreign resident or a temporary resident
      `section 115-102 or 115-125 applies to the gain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the asset is a new residential dwelling or affordable housing whose gain keeps the discount under s 115-102 or s 115-125
      `acquired on` IS A NUMBER @desc When you acquired the asset (YYYYMMDD)
      `event on` IS A NUMBER @desc When you sold it, or the CGT event happened (YYYYMMDD)
      `index number for the quarter of the CGT event` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number first published for the quarter of the sale
      `amounts` IS A LIST OF `Cost base amount` @desc Each amount in your cost base, as for the cost base question
      `capital proceeds` IS A NUMBER @desc What you receive for the asset, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Indexed answer`
`What is my capital gain on the indexed cost base` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What is my indexed cost base` `foreign or temporary resident in the testing period` `section 115-102 or 115-125 applies to the gain`
                                            `acquired on` `event on` `index number for the quarter of the CGT event` `amounts`
    WHEN `dollars` `cost base` THEN
        `dollars` (IF `capital proceeds` GREATER THAN `cost base` THEN `capital proceeds` MINUS `cost base` ELSE 0)
    OTHERWISE `not covered: an amount in the cost base was incurred or paid before 1 July 2027, or is not a (1C) amount`
